INSERT INTO sources VALUES(2,0,'hipparcos-2007','Hipparcos, the new reduction (van Leeuwen 2007)','vizier','stars','van Leeuwen F. 2007, "Validation of the new Hipparcos reduction", A&A 474, 653. 2007A&A...474..653V, doi:10.1051/0004-6361:20078357. Catalogue: van Leeuwen F. 2007, "Hipparcos, the New Reduction of the Raw Data", Astrophysics & Space Science Library 350; VizieR catalogue I/311.','https://cds.unistra.fr/vizier-org/licences_vizier.html','The VizieR Information System provides a standardized description of astronomical catalogues, and generally a free access to the data contained therein, essentially dedicated to a scientific usage. The data retrieved with VizieR are free of usage in a scientific context; however, as it is the usage in scientific publication, the original authors and publication references including the publisher have to be explicitely cited (see section Code of conduct of scientific research).','This research has made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI : 10.26093/cds/vizier). The original description of the VizieR service was published in 2000, A&AS 143, 23. Cite van Leeuwen 2007, A&A 474, 653.','permitted_with_credit','provisional',5,'{"method":"vizier_tsv","table":"I/311/hip2","constraints":[],"slices":{"column":"HIP","from":1,"to":120404,"step":30000},"rows":117955}','["No server-side cut: every row of I/311/hip2 (the astrometric catalogue), 117,955 by the ReadMe and as served.","Positions are RArad/DErad at their own epoch J1991.25 in ICRS, as the ReadMe states; VizieR''s header declares \"J2000_1991.250: eq_FK5 J2000\" for the table, and the ReadMe''s ICRS is taken.","Sn is the solution type of the new reduction (ReadMe Note 1: 10xd+s). The files are those of 16-Sep-2008, which correct errors in the June 2008 version.","B-V (with e_B-V) and V-I are the colour indices the ReadMe lists for the catalogue, in the Johnson B-V and Cousins V-I systems of the original Hipparcos catalogue; V-I has no error column."]','[{"defect":"RArad and DErad are named and documented in radians (the ReadMe gives unit \"rad\"), but VizieR serves them in degrees.","change":"RArad and DErad are read as degrees, as the answer''s units line gives them; no radian conversion is applied.","evidence":"I/311 ReadMe: RArad, DErad \"Right Ascension/Declination in ICRS, Ep=1991.25\", unit rad. The asu-tsv answer from vizieridia.saao.ac.za (2026-11-03) gives \"deg\" on its units line for both, and HIP 1 has RArad = 000.00091185, while VizieR''s _RAJ2000 for it is 000.0009007898 deg: the difference matches pmRA = -4.55 mas/yr over 8.75 yr only if RArad is in degrees.","action":null}]');
INSERT INTO sources VALUES(2,1,'hipparcos-1997','Hipparcos main catalogue spectral types (ESA 1997)','vizier','stars','ESA 1997, The Hipparcos and Tycho Catalogues, ESA SP-1200 (1997ESASP1200.....E).','https://cds.unistra.fr/vizier-org/licences_vizier.html','The VizieR Information System provides a standardized description of astronomical catalogues, and generally a free access to the data contained therein, essentially dedicated to a scientific usage. The data retrieved with VizieR are free of usage in a scientific context; however, as it is the usage in scientific publication, the original authors and publication references including the publisher have to be explicitely cited (see section Code of conduct of scientific research).','This research has made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI : 10.26093/cds/vizier). The original description of the VizieR service was published in 2000, A&AS 143, 23. Cite ESA 1997, The Hipparcos and Tycho Catalogues, ESA SP-1200 ("Credit: ESA").','permitted_with_credit','provisional',5,'{"method":"vizier_tsv","table":"I/239/hip_main","constraints":[],"slices":{"column":"HIP","from":1,"to":150000,"step":30000},"rows":118218}','["No server-side cut: every row of I/239/hip_main, 118,218 by the ReadMe (hip_main.dat, 118218 records).","Only HIP and SpType are taken: the spectral type of field H76 of the original Hipparcos catalogue, as published; the astrometry of the new reduction (van Leeuwen 2007) is taken from hipparcos-2007, to which each row is attached by its HIP number.","I/239 holds 118,218 records and I/311 117,955 (both ReadMes), so at least 263 HIP numbers have no Hipparcos-2 star to attach to: the stars the new reduction gave no solution. Each stands as an object of one entry, with its spectral type and no position or distance, found by its HIP designation and drawn in no tile."]','[]');
INSERT INTO sources VALUES(2,2,'mcconnachie-2012','McConnachie 2012 Local Group and nearby dwarf galaxies','vizier','nearby_galaxies','McConnachie A.W. 2012, "The observed properties of dwarf galaxies in and around the Local Group", AJ 144, 4. 2012AJ....144....4M, doi:10.1088/0004-6256/144/1/4. VizieR catalogue J/AJ/144/4, doi:10.26093/cds/vizier.51440004.','https://cds.unistra.fr/vizier-org/licences_vizier.html','The VizieR Information System provides a standardized description of astronomical catalogues, and generally a free access to the data contained therein, essentially dedicated to a scientific usage. The data retrieved with VizieR are free of usage in a scientific context; however, as it is the usage in scientific publication, the original authors and publication references including the publisher have to be explicitely cited (see section Code of conduct of scientific research).','This research has made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI : 10.26093/cds/vizier). The original description of the VizieR service was published in 2000, A&AS 143, 23. Cite McConnachie 2012, AJ 144, 4.','permitted_with_credit','provisional',5,'{"method":"vizier_tsv","table":"J/AJ/144/4/catalog","constraints":[],"slices":null,"rows":102}','["No server-side cut: every row of the catalog table (ReadMe table1.dat to table5.dat merged by VizieR), 102 by the ReadMe and as served.","This is the 2012 published version (ReadMe dated 24-Jul-2013), not the author''s continually updated online table.","Row 1, The Galaxy, has the position of Sgr A*.","All distance moduli come from resolved stellar populations (ReadMe Note 7). E_ columns are the positive and e_ columns the negative errors; u_(m-M) flags an uncertain or fixed distance and f_HRV flags the velocity (e.g. r: optical and HI velocities disagree)."]','[]');
INSERT INTO sources VALUES(2,3,'updated-nearby-galaxies','Updated Nearby Galaxy Catalog (Karachentsev et al. 2013)','vizier','nearby_galaxies','Karachentsev I.D., Makarov D.I., Kaisina E.I. 2013, "Updated nearby galaxy catalog", AJ 145, 101. 2013AJ....145..101K, doi:10.1088/0004-6256/145/4/101. VizieR catalogue J/AJ/145/101, doi:10.26093/cds/vizier.51450101.','https://cds.unistra.fr/vizier-org/licences_vizier.html','The VizieR Information System provides a standardized description of astronomical catalogues, and generally a free access to the data contained therein, essentially dedicated to a scientific usage. The data retrieved with VizieR are free of usage in a scientific context; however, as it is the usage in scientific publication, the original authors and publication references including the publisher have to be explicitely cited (see section Code of conduct of scientific research).','This research has made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI : 10.26093/cds/vizier). The original description of the VizieR service was published in 2000, A&AS 143, 23. Cite Karachentsev, Makarov & Kaisina 2013, AJ 145, 101.','permitted_with_credit','provisional',5,'{"method":"vizier_tsv","table":"J/AJ/145/101/catalog","constraints":[],"slices":null,"rows":869}','["The query takes every row of the catalog table (ReadMe table1.dat + table2.dat merged by VizieR), 869 by the ReadMe and as served.","Only measured distances are taken: on rows whose f_Dist is h or h'' (Hubble velocity-distance relation at H0 = 73 km/s/Mpc) or txt (likely proximity from texture; the ReadMe, Note (G1), says \"One of a small number of dwarf galaxies (N=11)\", read from http://vizier.nao.ac.jp/ftp/cats/J/AJ/145/101/ReadMe 2026-11-03, but the table as served marks 20 rows txt) the distance is an estimate, so it is dropped and the row kept, with its position, velocity and magnitude (fixes below).","Dist has no uncertainty in this table; it is marked as none reported (per-measurement e_DM is in table6, not taken).","a26, the \"Major angular diameter\" at the Holmberg isophote in the B band, in arcmin (ReadMe table1.dat, Note (1)), is taken under quality, as the model has no field for a size: the extent rule of the matching rules reads it as published, and it is blank on rows without one."]','[{"defect":"Dist mixes measured distances with estimates: on rows whose f_Dist is h or h'' it is derived from the velocity by the Hubble relation at H0 = 73 km/s/Mpc, and on rows marked txt it is a guess from the galaxy''s texture, not a measurement (110 rows as served).","change":"On those rows Dist is dropped and the entry kept: the galaxy is listed and matched by its position and velocity, and placed only by another source''s distance or redshift.","evidence":"J/AJ/145/101 ReadMe Note (G1) (read from http://vizier.nao.ac.jp/ftp/cats/J/AJ/145/101/ReadMe, 2026-11-03): h and h'' are distances \"by the Hubble velocity-distance relation at H0=73 km/s/Mpc\", and txt marks dwarfs whose \"texture ... indicates their likely proximity\". The definition keeps only measured distances; the rest of the row is as measured.","action":{"kind":"drop_when","columns":["Dist"],"when":{"column":"f_Dist","is":["h","h''","txt"]}}},{"defect":"The Milky Way''s row gives Dist = 0.01 Mpc (f_Dist geom): the Sun''s distance from the Galactic centre rounded to the table''s hundredth of a megaparsec, 10 kpc, 22% beyond the 8.18 kpc measured.","change":"The row keeps its published Dist and gains, beside it, the geometric distance of the Galactic centre that GRAVITY Collaboration 2019 measured, R0 = 8178 pc with an error of 25.6 pc (its 13 pc statistical and 22 pc systematic errors in quadrature); the entry is flagged with the citation. Its position, the direction of Sgr A*, is kept.","evidence":"The row as served by vizier.idia.ac.za on 2026-11-03: Name \"Milky Way\", _RAJ2000 266.416667, _DEJ2000 -29.007778, Dist 0.01, f_Dist geom, HRV 0, Bmag -4.60. GRAVITY Collaboration, Abuter R. et al. 2019, \"A geometric distance measurement to the Galactic Center black hole with 0.3% uncertainty\", A&A 625, L10 (arXiv 1904.05721), abstract: \"Our measurement uses the star S2 on its 16-year orbit around the massive black hole Sgr A* ... this yields a geometric distance estimate: R0 = 8178 +- 13(stat.) +- 22(sys.) pc.\"","action":{"kind":"add_distance","key":"Name","unit":"parsec","distance_kind":"geometric","method":{"other":"orbit of the star S2 about Sgr A*"},"measure":"euclidean","mark":{"flag":"distance_source","cite":"The Galactic centre''s distance R0 = 8178 +- 13 (stat) +- 22 (sys) pc is GRAVITY Collaboration, Abuter R. et al. 2019, A&A 625, L10, 2019A&A...625L..10G, arXiv 1904.05721, beside UNGC''s own Dist of 0.01 Mpc"},"values":{"Milky Way":[8178.0,25.6]}}}]');
INSERT INTO sources VALUES(2,4,'twomrs','2MASS Redshift Survey (2MRS) catalogue, ApJS journal table','vizier','cosmic_web','Huchra J.P., Macri L.M., Masters K.L., Jarrett T.H., Berlind P., Calkins M., Crook A.C., Cutri R., Erdogdu P., Falco E., et al. 2012, "The 2MASS Redshift Survey - Description and data release", ApJS 199, 26. 2012ApJS..199...26H, doi:10.1088/0067-0049/199/2/26. VizieR catalogue J/ApJS/199/26, doi:10.26093/cds/vizier.21990026.','https://cds.unistra.fr/vizier-org/licences_vizier.html','The VizieR Information System provides a standardized description of astronomical catalogues, and generally a free access to the data contained therein, essentially dedicated to a scientific usage. The data retrieved with VizieR are free of usage in a scientific context; however, as it is the usage in scientific publication, the original authors and publication references including the publisher have to be explicitely cited (see section Code of conduct of scientific research).','This research has made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI : 10.26093/cds/vizier). The original description of the VizieR service was published in 2000, A&AS 143, 23. Cite Huchra et al. 2012, ApJS 199, 26, and each entry''s redshift by its r_cz bibliographic code, as the team''s README terms (1) and (2) ask.','permitted_with_credit','provisional',5,'{"method":"vizier_tsv","table":"J/ApJS/199/26/table3","constraints":[],"slices":null,"rows":44599}','["No server-side cut: every row of table3 (the 2MRS catalog), 44,599 by the ReadMe and as served.","This is the VizieR copy of the journal table, not the team''s v2.4 files from tdc-www.cfa.harvard.edu.","cz and e_cz are nullable; a blank cz is a galaxy without a redshift, kept for its position.","cz is corrected to the solar system barycentre (ReadMe).","r_cz is the per-entry redshift reference (see table4) that the team''s terms ask users to cite. The model has no reference field, so it is taken under quality.","Riso, the \"Log of K=20 mag/sq arcsec elliptical isophote semimajor axis\" in [arcsec] (ReadMe table3.dat), is taken under quality, as the model has no field for a size: the extent rule of the matching rules reads it as published."]','[{"defect":"e_cz = 0 does not mean zero uncertainty: 788 rows give e_cz = 0, almost all with literature redshifts (260 from 2001ApJ...560..566K, 94 from 2005ApJS..160..149S, 28 from 1999PASP..111..438F, 25 from RC3, and others), whose sources gave no error.","change":"e_cz = 0 is read as no uncertainty reported, never as a zero uncertainty.","evidence":"The query J/ApJS/199/26/table3 with e_cz=0 on vizier.idia.ac.za (2026-11-03) returned 788 rows spread over many r_cz references; the ReadMe describes e_cz only as \"? Uncertainty in cz\", and a measured redshift never has an uncertainty of exactly zero.","action":{"kind":"zero_error_is_none_reported","columns":["e_cz"]}}]');
INSERT INTO sources VALUES(2,5,'cosmicflows-4','Cosmicflows-4 group distances','vizier','cosmic_web','Tully R.B., Kourkchi E., Courtois H.M., Anand G.S., Blakeslee J.P., Brout D., de Jaeger T., Dupuy A., Guinet D., Howlett C., et al. 2023, "Cosmicflows-4", ApJ 944, 94. 2023ApJ...944...94T, doi:10.3847/1538-4357/ac94d8. VizieR catalogue J/ApJ/944/94, doi:10.26093/cds/vizier.19440094. The positions of 148 groups that the table gives wrongly are those of Kourkchi E. & Tully R.B. 2017, "Galaxy groups within 3500 km/s", ApJ 843, 16, 2017ApJ...843...16K, VizieR catalogue J/ApJ/843/16 (fixes below).','https://cds.unistra.fr/vizier-org/licences_vizier.html','The VizieR Information System provides a standardized description of astronomical catalogues, and generally a free access to the data contained therein, essentially dedicated to a scientific usage. The data retrieved with VizieR are free of usage in a scientific context; however, as it is the usage in scientific publication, the original authors and publication references including the publisher have to be explicitely cited (see section Code of conduct of scientific research).','This research has made use of the VizieR catalogue access tool, CDS, Strasbourg, France (DOI : 10.26093/cds/vizier). The original description of the VizieR service was published in 2000, A&AS 143, 23. Cite Tully et al. 2023, ApJ 944, 94, and Kourkchi & Tully 2017, ApJ 843, 16, for the 148 group positions taken from it.','permitted_with_credit','provisional',5,'{"method":"vizier_tsv","table":"J/ApJ/944/94/groups","constraints":[],"slices":null,"rows":38053}','["No server-side cut: every row of the groups table (ReadMe table3.dat + table4.dat, merged by VizieR), 38,053 by the ReadMe and as served. The abstract says 38,065 groups; the 12-group difference is unexplained.","The individual-galaxy table J/ApJ/944/94/table2 (55,877 galaxies) is the source cosmicflows-4-galaxies.","DMzp is the group distance modulus on the scale of the TRGB, Cepheid and maser calibrators (ReadMe Note 1); Dist, derived from it, is not taken.","V3k, the group velocity relative to the cosmic background, is taken; Vh (relative to the Sun), Vls (the Local Sheet), fV3k (V3k times the curvature adjustment f) and the peculiar velocities are not."]','[{"defect":"SGX, SGY and SGZ are labelled Mpc in the ReadMe and by VizieR, but hold km/s: they are the Local Sheet velocity Vls times the supergalactic unit vector, positions in velocity space.","change":"SGX, SGY and SGZ are read as km/s (velocity-space supergalactic Cartesian coordinates), not as Mpc. No distance is taken from them.","evidence":"(1) The ReadMe contradicts itself: the unit column says Mpc while the description says \"Cartesian supergalactic coordinates of group, observed velocity units\"; VizieR serves the same unit and description. (2) The stated SGX range [-22455/23499] cannot be Mpc when the same table''s Dist range is [0.1/773] Mpc. (3) On 2,000 served rows (vizier.idia.ac.za, 2026-11-03) sqrt(SGX^2+SGY^2+SGZ^2) equals |Vls| within 2 km/s, e.g. 1PGC 12: Vls = 6669, (SGX, SGY, SGZ) = (1848, -6271, 1312), norm 6668; 1PGC 6830: Vls = -157, (40, 141, 56), norm 157.","action":{"kind":"read_as","columns":["SGX","SGY","SGZ"],"unit":"kilometre_per_second"}},{"defect":"157 group positions point away from the group in every position column of the groups table: RAdeg/DEdeg (served as _RAJ2000/_DEJ2000), GLON/GLAT, SGL/SGB and the SGX/SGY/SGZ derived from the same direction. No table2 member of these groups lies within 2 degrees of the group, and most lie 4-150 degrees away.","change":"For the 148 of them that share a 1PGC with the group catalogue of Kourkchi & Tully 2017 (ApJ 843, 16; VizieR J/ApJ/843/16/table2), from which the paper builds its groups, the position is replaced with Kourkchi & Tully''s group centre: the _RAJ2000 and _DEJ2000 that VizieR computes from that table''s GLON and GLAT (FK5 J2000), served by vizier.idia.ac.za on 2026-11-03 (http://vizier.idia.ac.za/viz-bin/asu-tsv?-source=J/ApJ/843/16/table2 with -out=PGC1,GLON,GLAT,SGLON,SGLAT and -out.add=_RAJ,_DEJ, one row for each 1PGC below). SGX, SGY and SGZ, the Local Sheet velocity along the wrong direction, are dropped on those rows rather than recomputed, as the definition does not take Vls: the group keeps its distance, velocity and corrected direction. The other 9 are left out under wrong_position (the next fix).","evidence":"(1) Tully et al. 2023 (Sec. XII) build the groups from Kourkchi & Tully 2017 first, and the ReadMe''s Note G1 names it as the source of 1PGC. Of the 2,498 groups that share a 1PGC with KT17 table2, 2,399 have SGL/SGB equal to KT17''s; 68 have SGL/SGB equal to KT17''s GLON/GLAT (galactic angles written as supergalactic), e.g. 1PGC 1816: KT17 GLON/GLAT 311.0300/-65.2643, CF4 SGL/SGB 311.0300/-65.2643, CF4 RA/Dec 79.5961/-8.3090 against its one table2 member at 7.4238/-51.5207 and KT17''s centre 7.4237/-51.5207; 80 others differ from KT17 by 4-119 degrees, e.g. 1PGC 41220 (Virgo): CF4 RA/Dec 220.8243/-23.9008, KT17 centre 187.7558/+12.4059, M49 (table2) 187.445/+8.000. (2) In every row the six angles and SGX/SGY/SGZ agree with each other (to 0.1 degree; SGX/SGY/SGZ to 1 degree) on the rows served by vizier.idia.ac.za on 2026-11-03, so VizieR computes _RAJ2000/_DEJ2000 correctly from RAdeg/DEdeg: the error is in the published table.","action":{"kind":"replace_by_key","key":"1PGC","columns":["_RAJ2000","_DEJ2000"],"drop":["SGX","SGY","SGZ"],"mark":{"flag":"position_source","cite":"The position is Kourkchi & Tully 2017''s group centre, not Cosmicflows-4''s wrong one: Kourkchi E. & Tully R.B. 2017, \"Galaxy groups within 3500 km/s\", ApJ 843, 16, 2017ApJ...843...16K; VizieR J/ApJ/843/16/table2, its _RAJ2000 and _DEJ2000 (FK5 J2000)"},"values":{"12838":[51.944587,-21.275534],"13265":[53.621567,-20.322988],"13418":[54.318359,-35.389696],"13419":[54.819585,-23.214126],"13505":[55.120401,-18.604365],"14526":[62.100571,-47.897104],"14558":[62.258089,-45.517682],"14